   CSS NOTES: Specificity (Conceptual Explanation)

   What is Specificity?
   -------------------
   CSS specificity decides which CSS rule is applied when
   multiple rules target the same element.

   It is about PRIORITY, not calculation.

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Why Specificity Exists
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   - Prevents conflicts between CSS rules
   - Helps browser choose the correct style
   - Makes styling predictable and controlled

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   How the Browser Decides (Conceptually)
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   When multiple rules match the same element, the browser
   checks priority in this order:

   1. Inline styles (highest priority)
   2. ID-based selectors
   3. Class, attribute, and pseudo-class selectors
   4. Element (tag) selectors (lowest priority)

   If two rules have the same priority,
   the rule written LAST wins.

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Specificity is About Target Accuracy
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   - More targeted selectors have more priority
   - Narrow context beats broad context

   Example:
   p              -> very general
   .card p        -> more specific
   #main .card p  -> very specific

   The browser prefers the rule that describes
   the element more precisely.

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Specificity vs Order
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   - Specificity is checked FIRST
   - Order matters ONLY when specificity is equal

   Later rules override earlier ones
   only if both have the same priority.


   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Best Practices
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   - Prefer classes over IDs
   - Avoid deeply nested selectors
   - Avoid !important
   - Write clean, predictable CSS

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   One-Line Summary
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Specificity decides which CSS rule wins based on how
   precisely it targets an element.

